 [rel('indigenous','Challenges a categorical boundary between Indigenous life and modernity through the case of Mary Sully’s art.',[sid('deloria_sully_qa')],'Primary written answer on being native to modernism, 2024. The argument concerns a distinctive artist and does not make her representative of all Indigenous people. The complete book remains unread.'),rel('publichistory','Explains a collaborative route from family-held drawings through historical research and public talks to museum interpretation.',[sid('deloria_sully_qa')],'Primary Q&A answers on rediscovery, curatorial challenges, book formation and exhibitions. Deloria credits his mother, audiences and named curators; this records historical/public interpretation, not sole creation of the art or a generic museum affiliation.')],
